WEBVTT

00:14:57.019 --> 00:15:00.635
But even if they wanted to reduce emissions,

00:15:00.635 --> 00:15:02.990
it will not happen overnight.

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:05.000
It will take some time.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.949
The immediate step for them

00:15:06.949 --> 00:15:09.350
would be to pay the tax.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.825
If they pay this additional tax,

00:15:11.825 --> 00:15:15.740
their overall cost of production will go up.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:18.169
Since their overall cost of

00:15:18.169 --> 00:15:20.270
production has gone up,

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.299
they automatically will try to pass

00:15:23.299 --> 00:15:27.019
this cost onto their customers.

00:15:27.019 --> 00:15:29.974
Consumers can be anyone -

00:15:29.974 --> 00:15:32.225
individuals, institutions,

00:15:32.225 --> 00:15:35.449
shopping malls, schools, shops.

00:15:35.449 --> 00:15:38.930
These consumers now must pay

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:43.110
a higher price for the same product.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:48.289
As a consumer, what choices do I have now?

00:15:48.289 --> 00:15:50.960
When the price of a product goes up,

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.300
what do we usually do?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.390
If it's not so necessary for us,

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.024
we usually stop using that product.

00:15:59.024 --> 00:16:02.950
If possible, switch to another product.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.439
Stop using or switching

00:16:05.439 --> 00:16:07.629
to another product might not be

00:16:07.629 --> 00:16:09.744
an option if this product

00:16:09.744 --> 00:16:12.760
is a necessity, like electricity.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.875
But in this case,

00:16:14.875 --> 00:16:17.754
we have plenty of other options.

00:16:17.754 --> 00:16:21.355
Option 1 is to save electricity,

00:16:21.355 --> 00:16:24.010
so I will have to pay less.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.875
Option 2 would be

00:16:26.875 --> 00:16:30.070
to switch my electricity providers.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.890
If my present electricity provider

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:35.260
increases tariffs because he

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.135
has to pay a carbon tax,

00:16:37.135 --> 00:16:38.889
which means he's

00:16:38.889 --> 00:16:41.814
generating electricity from fossil fuels,

00:16:41.814 --> 00:16:44.350
I can try to find a provider who is

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.785
generating electricity from clean sources.

00:16:47.785 --> 00:16:50.170
He will not be paying carbon tax

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.639
and might be able to sell

00:16:51.639 --> 00:16:56.184
electricity at relatively cheaper prices.

00:16:56.184 --> 00:17:00.039
Option 3, especially if I'm

00:17:00.039 --> 00:17:01.930
a shopping mall establishment,

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.584
a school or any other institution,

00:17:04.584 --> 00:17:06.190
I can invest in

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.099
my own clean energy-generating system,

00:17:09.099 --> 00:17:11.290
such as solar PVs.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.739
I will have my own solar system on my roof,

00:17:14.739 --> 00:17:17.290
generating my own electricity.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:19.840
No longer will I be required to buy

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:21.894
expensive electricity

00:17:21.894 --> 00:17:24.685
from my regular retailer.

00:17:24.685 --> 00:17:27.369
When everyone starts taking

00:17:27.369 --> 00:17:29.049
one of these approaches,

00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:31.600
starts switching to clean power,

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.750
this will create demand in the market and

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.879
make clean energy investments

00:17:36.879 --> 00:17:38.709
more profitable.

00:17:38.709 --> 00:17:41.590
It will even create incentives for

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:44.080
carbon-intensive industries to

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.899
shift towards clean alternatives.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:52.510
In the longer term, emissions will fall.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:55.614
The story doesn't end here.

00:17:55.614 --> 00:17:57.879
The government will generate

00:17:57.879 --> 00:18:01.330
huge revenues from carbon taxes.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:05.829
Using these revenues wisely is the key here.

00:18:05.829 --> 00:18:07.519
Governments can use

00:18:07.519 --> 00:18:10.384
these revenues to compensate

00:18:10.384 --> 00:18:12.710
the low-income families for

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:13.909
the increased cost of

00:18:13.909 --> 00:18:16.234
electricity and other services.

00:18:16.234 --> 00:18:18.560
Or they can invest in

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.345
climate protection projects

00:18:20.345 --> 00:18:22.325
or other public projects,

00:18:22.325 --> 00:18:24.899
such as healthcare for all.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:30.665
The carbon tax is a well-designed tool

00:18:30.665 --> 00:18:34.714
that can help us achieve three goals at once.

00:18:34.714 --> 00:18:38.149
First, by putting a price on carbon,

00:18:38.149 --> 00:18:41.029
we ensure emissions go down

00:18:41.029 --> 00:18:43.355
and polluters pay.

00:18:43.355 --> 00:18:46.834
Second, we create financial incentives

00:18:46.834 --> 00:18:49.545
for switching to clean energy.

00:18:49.545 --> 00:18:52.539
Finally, the government generates

00:18:52.539 --> 00:18:54.129
revenue that can be

00:18:54.129 --> 00:18:58.070
used for climate protection programmes.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:02.259
These are some of the

00:19:02.259 --> 00:19:04.945
existing carbon pricing initiatives

00:19:04.945 --> 00:19:06.429
around the world.

00:19:06.429 --> 00:19:09.144
Most of them are already implemented,

00:19:09.144 --> 00:19:12.760
some are scheduled for under consideration.

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.204
We talked about technology,

00:19:15.204 --> 00:19:17.170
we talked about policy.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.090
Even with plenty of

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.595
technologies and policy tools,

00:19:21.595 --> 00:19:24.160
we haven't made much progress in

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.520
our quest to mitigate climate change.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:30.069
That brings me to talk about

00:19:30.069 --> 00:19:33.097
the economics of climate change.




